# Normalise line endings in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true` gets
# CRLF in its working tree, and the golden strategy charts stop matching what
# the engine renders. That turned the §14.4 regression guard into a test that
# failed on Windows and passed on Linux, for reasons with nothing to do with the
# charts it is meant to be guarding.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberately unconditional rather than a `-text` exemption for the
# golden files: marking them binary stops git normalising them at all, which
# means a commit made on Windows would quietly store CRLF and move the problem
# rather than fix it.
* text=auto eol=lf
